{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`. I judged this from the supplied test source and did not read any implementation.\n\n- **Separate record per run at `<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json`:**\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` checks that the file is named `<run_id>.json` and sits under `habeas/authoring/usage` in the state root.\n  - The same test runs a second time with `--force` and asserts that the first record's bytes are unchanged and that two files exist.\n  - `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record]` and `citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` check separate records with distinct run ids.\n- **Required fields:**\n  - `usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported` asserts `version` is 3, plus `run_id`, `project_root`, `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend`, `model`, `evidence_output` and `start_time_ms <= end_time_ms`.\n  - `usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind` asserts that the subject kind is recorded when the run fails before sources are prepared, with null backend and model and a set end time.\n  - `usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared` covers the requirement, example, citation review and site review kinds.\n  - `src/authoring/usage.rs#fn[unfinished_runs_are_visible_before_the_backend_is_selected]` asserts null backend, model and end time for an unfinished run.\n- **Determination kind when present:**\n  - `true` is asserted in `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files`.\n  - `false` is asserted in `false_is_a_completed_assessment`.\n  - `FIXME` is asserted in `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free`, and in `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage`.\n  - A null determination is asserted for failed runs in `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence` and `failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause`.\n- **`evidence_output` and `evidence_written`:**\n  - File mode: `evidence_output` is `file` and `evidence_written` is true in the Ollama CLI tests and the batch tests.\n  - Stdout mode: `evidence_output` is `stdout` and `evidence_written` is true, asserted for the true, false and FIXME determinations in `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` and in `live_bedrock_authoring`.\n  - Failed submissions record `evidence_written` as false, with the matching destination, in both modes in `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence`.\n  - A failed evidence write records false in `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage`.\n- **Usage outside the project in stdout mode:** `usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it` runs with and without `--stdout`. It asserts that a state root inside the project is refused with the \"must be outside the project repository\" message and is not created. The stdout-mode usage file is shown to exist at the reported path in `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files`.\n- **No FIXME entry text:** the Ollama test asserts that the serialized usage record does not contain \"#125\".\n- **Failed, cancelled and unfinished runs are distinguishable from completed ones:**\n  - `outcome` is \"failed\" in the batch failure tests and in `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence`.\n  - `failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause` asserts \"failed\" for a `PermissionDenied` error and \"cancelled\" for an `Interrupted` error, with a null determination and a set end time.\n  - `outcome` is \"unfinished\" in `unfinished_runs_are_visible_before_the_backend_is_selected`.\n  - `interrupted_terminal_progress_keeps_unstarted_work_incomplete` covers an interrupted batch.\n  - Completed runs assert \"completed\".\n- **No source text, prompts, responses or rationale:** the Ollama test asserts that the usage record contains none of `SECRET_REQUIREMENT_TEXT`, `SECRET_DEFINITION_TEXT`, `SECRET_SOURCE_PAYLOAD`, `SECRET_RATIONALE` or the credential. The workspace-configuration test also asserts that the literal API key is absent from usage.\n- **Cited `requirements.configuration.state_location`:** `usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported` shows the records created under the state root. It also shows that an unusable `XDG_STATE_HOME` (a file blocking the path) or a missing `XDG_STATE_HOME` and `HOME` makes the command fail with stderr output, no stdout and no evidence rewritten.\n\nThe remaining tests marked for this requirement (the batch, provider, adaptive and persistence tests) reinforce these assertions. I found no acknowledgments or exemptions to weigh.",
  "references": "8c266bd14ae66b5b7651841b71fae50faddc6c6ad08ec107580bad7462d9a96b",
